title: Rerender views
pid: bd991797-7e52-4967-aa83-94717707ada9
body: |2-
    - Request: =((request . "rerender views") (view-ids "VIEW_ID" ...)
      (approved-overPrivateText-pids "PID" ...))=. =view-ids= is
      required; the approval is optional.
    - Response: a rerender stream (see "Rerender all views") of the
      open views named: each is refreshed from what the connection
      holds for it, a buffer of the diff view over the graph straddle,
      and not extended. A named view the connection does not hold adds
      an error to =rerender-done=; a request without =view-ids= gets an
      empty rerender stream whose =rerender-done= carries the error.
    - Writes nothing. Its use is to release a save's withheld rerender:
      the save's =overPrivateText-telescope-confirmation= names the views
      (see "Save buffer"), and the client sends this request for them,
      approving the PIDs that confirmation listed. Both clients and
      skg-for-ai do.
    - Under a restricted set, overPrivateText content without exact
      approval returns LP =overPrivateText-telescope-confirmation= with
      =(operation rerender-views)= and the exact PIDs, followed by an
      empty rerender stream; no view text is sent and no open-view
      registry entry changes. A retry with those PIDs is released; the
      release, or an unrestricted connection, adds the shared warning to
      =rerender-done=.
    - =server/serve/handlers/rerender_views.rs=.
